    #     the fp16/bf16 rounding quantum, one fewer FMA than the fp32 path.
    #   else (fp32): degree-9 (5 coeffs, max abs err ~1.2e-5) — needed for the
    #     tight fp32 rtol; a degree-7 fit only reaches ~1.4e-4 and fails atol.
    # NATIVE (fp16 only): evaluate the whole poly in the operand's 2-byte dtype
    #   instead of promoting to fp32; ~13% faster and still 0 bad elements at
    #   atol=1e-4/rtol=1e-3 (verified over 24 draws). bf16 shows no speedup and
    #   fp32 needs full precision, so both keep NATIVE=False (fp32 arithmetic).
    # Verified on dense grids and edge cases (all quadrants, signed zero,
    # large/tiny magnitudes; no NaN/Inf).
